I've found the relevant code in `HeaderView.tsx`. Specifically, the `threeDotMenuItems` array is being populated with the "Leave" menu item.

Here's the relevant snippet:

```typescript
if (ReportUtils.canLeaveChat(report, policy)) {
    const isWorkspaceMemberLeavingWorkspaceRoom = !isChatThread && (report.visibility === CONST.REPORT.VISIBILITY.RESTRICTED || isPolicyExpenseChat) && isPolicyEmployee;
    threeDotMenuItems.push({
        icon: Expensicons.ChatBubbles,
        text: translate('common.leave'),
        onSelected: Session.checkIfActionIsAllowed(() => Report.leaveRoom(reportID, isWorkspaceMemberLeavingWorkspaceRoom)),
    });
}
```

The `onSelected` handler directly calls `Report.leaveRoom`. This is different from the behavior on the group details page, which shows a confirmation modal. The fix is to show a confirmation modal before calling `Report.leaveRoom`.

I will now find the component that uses the `leave` button. The `ReportParticipantsPage.tsx` will be a good file to check.

